From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:52:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: Run the Linux build, lint and QuickJS jobs on the
 self-hosted runners

The x86_64 Linux build, the lint job and the QuickJS build now run on the
self-hosted runners labelled servo-ohos-linux. Their image has a checkout
and a target directory prebuilt at a recent ohos-main with the commands
and environment of these jobs, so cargo only rebuilds what a change
touches. On GitHub-hosted runners, the build with unit tests takes 37 to
57 minutes, the lint job 19 to 24 and the QuickJS build 18.

An expression chooses the runner, instead of servo's runner-select
action, which asks servo's own CI servers for a runner and so always fell
back to GitHub-hosted runners here. Pull requests from forks, the arm64
build (no self-hosted-image-name) and runs while the repository variable
NO_SELF_HOSTED_RUNNERS is set use GitHub-hosted runners. There is no
fallback while no self-hosted runner is online: the jobs wait for one,
and setting NO_SELF_HOSTED_RUNNERS sends later jobs to GitHub-hosted
runners. The job names lose the runner-select id.

On self-hosted runners the jobs don't install LLVM: the image has the
same release, and a download into runner.temp would change
LIBCLANG_PATH, which a build script watches, and so rebuild most of the
target directory. They don't set up sccache either, and the QuickJS build
also skips the setup steps that the other two jobs already skip there.

Pull requests from branches of this repository ran on GitHub-hosted runners.
`github.event.pull_request.head.repo.fork` is the head repository's fork
flag, and servo-ohos is a fork of servo/servo, so it is true for every pull
request. Compare the head repository with this one instead; without a pull
request (push, schedule, merge queue, dispatch) the runner stays self-hosted.

Validation: actionlint reports nothing new for the three workflows (its findings exist on ohos-main too), and `./mach test-tidy` passes. pr_jobs chooses Linux (unit tests, WPT), Lint, OpenHarmony and Linux QuickJS for this change, so its pull request runs all three jobs on the self-hosted runners and WPT tests the build from there. The runner image was built from ohos-main a02f323f8bf. In a container of it, in the jobs' workspace and with their environment, the jobs' commands compiled nothing for the build (crown, -D warnings), clippy (CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0, as lint.yml sets it) and the QuickJS build; the unit tests took 7 s (1068 tests); after a one-line change in the script crate, the build recompiled script, layout, servo and servoshell in 65 s on 32 cores. Two runners are online, but no job has run on them yet. Pull requests from branches of this repository: PR #25 (branch of this repository, Main run 38135694194) ran its Lint, Linux Build (x86_64) and Linux Build (QuickJS) jobs on ubuntu-22.04, and the API reports `"fork": true` for openharmony-rs/servo-ohos. actionlint 1.7.12 reports nothing new for the three workflows.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written by the agent, which also built and tested the runner image these jobs use)
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; diagnosed from the PR's job data and written by the agent)
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; 2026-10-13 sync -- folded in "squash! ci: Run the Linux build, lint and QuickJS jobs on the self-hosted runners" (the fork check for pull requests from branches of this repository))
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
